[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mShip GitOps-Ready Local Cluster Runtime Contract\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Deliver epic `VFHmKH5XR` so `port cluster up --cluster demo` produces a real single-node local K3s control plane rather than the current demo API surface. (\u001b[2mVFHmKH5XR\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - `port cluster kubeconfig --cluster demo --format json` returns a kubeconfig that works for normal Kubernetes clients without downstream rewriting. (\u001b[2muse the handed-off kubeconfig with standard Kubernetes clients from the host\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-03\u001b[0m - `kubectl api-resources -o name` against the handed-off kubeconfig includes at least `deployments.apps`, `namespaces`, `serviceaccounts`, `secrets`, `configmaps`, and `customresourcedefinitions.apiextensions.k8s.io`. (\u001b[2minspect API discovery from the handed-off kubeconfig\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-04\u001b[0m - `flux install` succeeds against the handed-off local kubeconfig. (\u001b[2mrun `flux install` against the Port-provided kubeconfig\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-05\u001b[0m - `helm upgrade --install pulumi-kubernetes-operator ...` succeeds against the same handed-off kubeconfig. (\u001b[2mrun the operator install against the Port-provided kubeconfig\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFHmKH5XR\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Replace Demo Local Cluster Stub With Real K3s Runtime (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-29T12:25:13\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFHmKGaXQ/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Ship GitOps-Ready Local Cluster Runtime Contract - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Deliver epic `VFHmKH5XR` so `port cluster up --cluster demo` produces a real single-node local K3s control plane rather than the current demo API surface. | board: VFHmKH5XR |\r\n| MG-02 | `port cluster kubeconfig --cluster demo --format json` returns a kubeconfig that works for normal Kubernetes clients without downstream rewriting. | manual: use the handed-off kubeconfig with standard Kubernetes clients from the host |\r\n| MG-03 | `kubectl api-resources -o name` against the handed-off kubeconfig includes at least `deployments.apps`, `namespaces`, `serviceaccounts`, `secrets`, `configmaps`, and `customresourcedefinitions.apiextensions.k8s.io`. | manual: inspect API discovery from the handed-off kubeconfig |\r\n| MG-04 | `flux install` succeeds against the handed-off local kubeconfig. | manual: run `flux install` against the Port-provided kubeconfig |\r\n| MG-05 | `helm upgrade --install pulumi-kubernetes-operator ...` succeeds against the same handed-off kubeconfig. | manual: run the operator install against the Port-provided kubeconfig |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Scope stays local-only and single-node only.\r\n- Do not add AWS, hosted-cluster, or multi-node orchestration in this mission.\r\n- Do not add ingress or load-balancer work unless it is strictly required for a real local single-node K3s control plane to function.\r\n- Keep Port as the owner of cluster bring-up, readiness, kubeconfig handoff, and API reachability; do not push GitOps prerequisites back into downstream guest choreography.\r\n- Downstream consumer verification is a follow-on concern outside this Port mission.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while the local cluster still behaves like a demo API or while Flux or Helm remain blocked on shortcomings in Port's local cluster contract.\r\n- HALT when epic `VFHmKH5XR` is done and manual verification confirms normal Kubernetes API discovery, `flux install`, and the Pulumi operator Helm install against the Port-handed kubeconfig.\r\n- YIELD if the remaining blocker requires a product decision on local guest networking, Kubernetes distribution choice, or non-local scope expansion rather than implementation work.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFHmKH5XR\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mReplace Demo Local Cluster Stub With Real K3s Runtime\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-29 12:20:10\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-29 12:27:56\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-29 17:14:22\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-29 17:14:22\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m4h 46m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFHmKH5XR/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFHmKH5XR/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port's current local cluster handoff is good enough for cluster up and kubeconfig, but it is still a demo API rather than a GitOps-capable single-node K3s control plane. Flux install, Helm operator install, and broad API discovery are not credible until the local lane is a real K3s runtime rather than a stub.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Replace the demo local cluster surface with a real single-node local K3s runtime that supports normal Kubernetes clients and GitOps bootstrap tooling. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport\u001b[0m hands off a kubeconfig that supports Kubernetes discovery plus Flux and Helm installs -> \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mflux install\u001b[0m and Helm operator install pass against the handed-off kubeconfig)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Preserve the intentionally narrow local-first boundary while closing the GitOps-readiness gap. (All execution and proof remain local-only and single-node only -> No AWS, hosted-cluster, or multi-node work lands in this epic)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport cluster up --cluster demo\u001b[0m must bring up a real single-node local K3s control plane rather than the current demo API surface.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFHmctWC5\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport cluster kubeconfig --cluster demo --format json\u001b[0m must hand off a kubeconfig that works for standard Kubernetes clients without downstream rewriting.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFHmctWC5\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkubectl api-resources -o name\u001b[0m against the handed-off kubeconfig must include at least \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mdeployments.apps\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mnamespaces\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mserviceaccounts\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61msecrets\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mconfigmaps\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcustomresourcedefinitions.apiextensions.k8s.io\u001b[0m.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFHmctWC5\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mflux install\u001b[0m and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mhelm upgrade --install pulumi-kubernetes-operator ...\u001b[0m must succeed against the same handed-off kubeconfig.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFHmctWC5\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Scope remains local-only and single-node only throughout this epic.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFHmctWC5\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Port remains the owner of cluster bring-up, readiness, kubeconfig handoff, and API reachability; downstream repos do not reintroduce manual guest orchestration or kubeconfig rewriting.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFHmctWC5\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - Verification must include direct Kubernetes discovery, Flux install, and Helm install rather than Port-only surface checks.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFHmctWC5\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              3/3 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m3/3\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - GitOps bootstrap clients: Live \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mflux install\u001b[0m and Helm operator install against the handed-off kubeconfig\r\n    - Real K3s control plane: Live \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport cluster up/status/kubeconfig\u001b[0m plus \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkubectl api-resources\u001b[0m and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkubectl get nodes\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 0 | manual 6\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 0 | manual 6\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 18 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFHmctWC5\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Replace Demo API With GitOps-Capable Local K3s Runtime (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
